    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Find two numbers such that the sum of their squares is 74 and their sum is 12.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$5$ and $7$.",
      "worked": "Let one number be $x$. The other number is $12-x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+(12-x)^2&=74\\\\2x^2-24x+144&=74\\\\2x^2-24x+70&=0\\\\x^2-12x+35&=0\\\\(x-5)(x-7)&=0\\\\x&=5\\text{ or }x=7\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe other number is respectively $7$ or $5$, so the two numbers are $5$ and $7$.\n\nCheck: $5+7=12$ and $5^2+7^2=25+49=74$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
